        "original_id": "f75d9359-eb85-5dda-8939-8275ccf5a1e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dal Lake, Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, Waterton Lake, Alberta, Montana, Canada, United States\n- Products: shikara\n- Buildings: Goathaunt Bunkhouse\n\nFacts:\n- Dal Lake is a lake in Srinagar, the summer capital of Jammu and Kashmir.\n- In Kashmiri, “Dal” means “lake,” so the name “Dal Lake” is a misnomer.\n- Waterton Lake is a mountain lake in southern Alberta, Canada, and northern Montana, United States.\n- A shikara is a type of wooden boat found on Dal Lake and other water bodies of Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, India.\n- Goathaunt Bunkhouse is near the southern end of Waterton Lake.\n- Goathaunt Bunkhouse is the last surviving structure of its era at that location.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
